To create a JSON object with the key `items` and set its value to be an array, you can use JavaScript or any other programming language that supports JSON manipulation.

Here's how you can do it in different languages:

### JavaScript

```javascript
const items = ["item1", "item2", "item3"];
const json = {
  items: items
};

console.log(json);
```

### Python (using `json` module)

```python
import json

items = ["item1", "item2", "item3"]
json_data = {"items": items}

print(json.dumps(json_data))
```

### Java

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import org.json.JSONObject;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<String> items = new ArrayList<>();
        items.add("item1");
        items.add("item2");
        items.add("item3");

        JSONObject jsonObject = new JSONObject();
        jsonObject.put("items", items);

        System.out.println(jsonObject.toString());
    }
}
```

